cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite as below."
title: "ARS — Arithmetic Resonance Spectrograph"
abstract: >
  A calibrated multi-scale random-matrix-theory readout for arbitrary time
  series. Embeds a sequence into a chirp signal, runs a GPU-parallel bank
  of Farey-rational phase-locked loops against it, and extracts passage-time
  spacings that are unfolded and compared against random matrix theory
  predictions (Wigner GOE / GUE / Poisson). Validated against the Riemann
  ζ zeros and the Katz–Sarnak family symmetry of elliptic curve L-functions.
  The repository also contains llmspec/, "Shapes of LLM weights over
  training": a pre-registered study of language-model weight spectra across
  training (Pythia 70M–1.4B with PolyPythias seeds, OLMo 2 1B), with five
  own 70M training runs comparing learning-rate warmups and AdamW vs Muon
  (Arm B). Code is AGPL-3.0-or-later; llmspec results and write-ups are
  CC-BY-4.0 (llmspec/LICENSE-RESULTS.md).
