  # ─── Foundational Planat-and-collaborators series ────────────────────────
  # ARS rests on the analytical scaffolding developed in this series across
  # Farey-rational phase locking, Ramanujan-Fourier analysis of arithmetical
  # signals, and the connection of arithmetic to oscillator phase noise.
  # Reference metadata below is the best available without an authoritative
  # CITATION-AUDIT.md; specific titles and journal identifiers should be
  # confirmed against the source list when one is provided.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Planat
        given-names: M.
      - family-names: Henry
        given-names: E.
    title: "Arithmetic of phase locking and 1/f noise in oscillators (Farey-Stern–Brocot organization of mode locking)"
    year: 2002
    notes: "FEMTO-ST.  Foundational treatment of PLL phase-noise via Farey arithmetic and continued-fraction expansions; ARS reuses this organization as the PLL-bank parameterization."
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Planat
        given-names: M.
      - family-names: Rosu
        given-names: H.
    title: "Ramanujan sums and the Ramanujan-Fourier expansion of arithmetical signals"
    year: 2002
    notes: "Foundational formulation of RF coefficient analysis on point processes / arithmetic functions; ARS Engine 1 (ramanujan_fourier) implements this directly."
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Planat
        given-names: M.
    title: "Phase locking, Mangoldt function, and connections to the Riemann zeta function"
    year: 2006
    notes: "Develops the analytical relation between Farey-rational phase locking and the von Mangoldt arithmetic function / Riemann ζ; the analytical anchor for ARS's Riemann-side validation."
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Planat
        given-names: M.
    title: "Bost–Connes / KMS-state perspective on rational-frequency phase coherence and prime-theoretic invariants (recent work)"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Recent work on the quantum statistical mechanics of phase-locking on rational frequencies; the analytical hypothesis that ARS's empirical Phase 12 perturbation sweep was originally framed against (with the Phase 13 reinterpretation noting that the Phase 12 signal is a peak-detection artifact, not a test of this hypothesis)."
